      "text": "29",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gLTyV",
      "text": "23",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & x^2 f^{\\prime}(x)-2 x f(x)=3 \\\\ & \\left(\\frac{x^2 f^{\\prime}(x)-2 x f(x)}{\\left(x^2\\right)^2}\\right)=\\frac{3}{\\left(x^2\\right)^2} \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\frac{d}{d x}\\left(\\frac{f(x)}{x^2}\\right)=\\frac{3}{x^4}\\end{aligned}$\n\n\nIntegrating both sides\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\frac{f(x)}{x^2}=-\\frac{1}{x^3}+C \\\\\n& f(x)=-\\frac{1}{x}+C x^2 \\\\\n& \\text { put } x=1 \\\\\n& 4=-1+C \\Rightarrow C=5 \\\\\n& f(x)=-\\frac{1}{x}+5 x^2 \\\\\n& \\text { Now } 2 \\times f(2)=2 \\times\\left[-\\frac{1}{2}+5 \\times 2^2\\right] \\\\\n& =39\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
